# ── Code Signing (Windows) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required for production builds. Obtain an EV Code Signing certificate from
# a trusted CA (DigiCert, Sectigo, GlobalSign, etc.) and export as .pfx file.
#
# electron-builder reads these automatically during `npm run build:win`.

# Path to your .pfx certificate file (absolute path recommended)
# WIN_CSC_LINK=/path/to/certificate.pfx

# Password for the .pfx certificate
# WIN_CSC_KEY_PASSWORD=your-certificate-password

# ── Optional: Azure Trusted Signing (alternative to PFX) ─────────────────────
# Recommended for CI/CD pipelines — no .pfx file needed on the build machine.
# Requires @electron/windows-sign package.
#
# AZURE_TENANT_ID=
# AZURE_CLIENT_ID=
# AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# AZURE_CODE_SIGNING_ACCOUNT_NAME=
# AZURE_CODE_SIGNING_PROFILE_NAME=
# AZURE_TRUSTED_SIGNING_ENDPOINT=
